o seemed a  bit forced as there wasn't much time for  character development in this movie's 1  hour and 52 minute run time the fight  sequences with abomination don't do much  for me because the stakes aren't very  high and because we don't see much of  the impact or aftermath of the  destruction their battles cause  you could also tell that the screenplay  had some issues which weren't wholly  resolved there are rumors that there was  some kind of dispute between ed norton  and zach penn on different rewrites of  the screenplay and i feel like some of  the dialogue and plot development  suffered from this  although the movie had some flaws it  also had some great things going for it  the editing the pacing and the  performance by ed norton are all  fantastic  coming in at number five on today's list  is iron man 2.  [Music]  this movie has plenty to love including  ivan venko's bird tony stark's drunken  djing and justin hammer's dance moves  but first let's talk about the few flaws  with this film  in the beginning i had little sympathy  for ivan or whiplash because again there  was very little time for character  development on his end it also seems a  bit rushed to immediately put him  against the great tony stark without  much of a plan other than to make it so  that the world can see tony bleed  it also seems like many of the early  marvel films failed to accomplish the  task of making empathetic villains but  they certainly do so with many of the  later films my biggest issue with this  movie though is the fact that tony cures  his blood toxicity by creating a new  element that his dad hid in an expo  layout mock-up  like what kind of lemony snicket sort of  stuff is that i mean if my dad wanted me  to figure out how to create something as  simple as a birdhouse he would at least  leave me with an instruction book  anyways this movie did have plenty of  good things going for it too one of my  favorite scenes is when tony puts on the  iron man suit in the brie