ranslation of the comic  villain to the screen is done in such a  great nostalgic way you can almost see  jack kirby's pen touching the screen  although this movie has plenty to love  there are still two phase one titles  which beat it out  i'm gonna do this all day  coming in at number two on today's list  is the avengers  doth mother know  you whereas her drapes  the sixth film in the mcu franchise the  avengers was probably one of the most  ambitious film crossovers of all time  when it was released rivaled only by one  this movie is fantastic bringing all the  characters we have gotten to know from  the previous five films together for an  epic show stopping innovation of a film  there's so many great things in this  movie i love how loki uses the scepter  to drive the characters apart i love how  steve rogers is continually impressed by  modern technology and advancements i  love how the helicarrier becomes  invisible as it lifts into the air and i  love all of the actors performances both  individually and as a group a lot of  times in in movies with a large cast  there doesn't seem to be much chemistry  between the main characters that is  absolutely not the case with the  avengers the way they bounce off of one  another and work together to stop loki  before eating some shawarma is just so  much fun to watch there are too many  great scenes to go through in this video  but i'll leave you with this  if you ever want to understand any of  the later mcu films you must watch the  avengers  and i will not be bullied by that  [Applause]  and finally coming in at number one on  today's list is iron man  for your consideration  the jericho  iron man geez i just don't know where to  start  this movie was and still is an absolute  masterpiece in storytelling in character  development in cinematography and  computer graphics and in talent  selection  i don't think many people thought robert  downey jr was the best choice for the  character of tony stark when the movie 